            <ArticleTitle>A dual blood supply protects the right gastroepiploic arterial graft: report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two cases whose right gastroepiploic arterial bypass grafts were protected by a dual blood supply due to the anatomical anastomosis between the celiac and the superior mesenteric artery systems. This unique characteristic of the graft adds an advantage for its use as a graft conduit.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
